{"type":"assistant","uuid":"b1d9f4ce-bda4-4120-a321-955ead00400d","session_id":"fab1830e-aa74-488e-8a22-42b2dc0b9084","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"b1d9f4ce-bda4-4120-a321-955ead00400d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash:0731-cloud","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The setup_overview returned `setup_assignment_clarification_required`. The server says: \"There are more requested board names than visible debug connections. Clarify which requested boards are currently attached before setup or validation; do not expose machine IDs.\"\n\nInteresting â€” I requested 2 board names (STM-A, STM-B) but the server says there are more requested board names than visible debug connections. The serial_choices show 4 VCOM ports:\n- COM17: STLink VCOM, identifier ending 213913 â†’ matches STM-B probe `0668FF514988525067213913`\n- COM12: STLink VCOM, identifier ending 233337 â†’ matches STM-A probe `066FFF514988525067233337`\n- COM15: JLink CDC UART, `000683854191` (Nordic nRF52840 board â€” not owned by this test)\n- COM16: JLink CDC UART, `000683710208` (Nordic â€” not owned)\n\nThe server's message says \"more requested board names than visible debug connections\" â€” but there are 4 serial choices visible. Hmm, the \"connections\" array is empty and \"profiles\" is empty. The server may be counting debug connections (probes) rather than VCOM ports. The two ST-Link probes are visible via their VCOM ports (COM12, COM17). The J-Link ones are the Nordic boards (not owned by S10).\n\nWait â€” the message says \"There are more requested board names than visible debug connections.\" I requested 2 names. If only... hmm, actually maybe the server counts the two ST-Link VCOM ports as the visible debug connections for STM boards, and the J-Link ones as unrelated. So 2 requested names vs 2 visible STM connections should match. But the server returned clarification required.\n\nActually, re-reading: \"There are more requested board names than visible debug connections.\" Perhaps the server's inventory of *debug connections* (probes) is empty because the serial_choices are VCOM ports, not debug probes. The `connections: []` array is empty. So the server sees 0 debug connections but 2 requested board names â†’ clarification required.\n\nThe server instructs: \"Clarify which requested boards are currently attached before setup or validation; do not expose machine IDs.\"\n\nPer the zero-operator policy, I cannot ask the user. But the resource assignment supplies the facts: STM-A probe `066FFF514988525067233337`/COM12 and STM-B probe `0668FF514988525067213913`/COM17 are the declared attached boards. The serial_choices confirm both ST-Link VCOM ports are present with exactly those stable USB identities. The J-Link ports (COM15, COM16) belong to the Nordic boards which are NOT owned by this test (HIL owns STM-A, STM-B only; \"it does not own Nordic resources\").\n\nThe server's clarification request is about which requested boards are currently attached. The manager-supplied electronic identities in RESOURCE_ASSIGNMENT.md are the authoritative facts: both STM-A and STM-B are attached (their probes/VCOMs are enumerated). The two J-Link VCOM ports are unrelated visible probes that \"do not need board names\" per the server's own guidance.\n\nSo how do I clarify without asking the user? The server's setup_overview accepts `connection_assignments` as a parameter! Looking at the tool schema: `setup_overview(board_names, connection_assignments)`. The `connection_assignments` is an object. I can pass the assignment mapping familiar names to the stable USB identities from the resource assignment.\n\nThe tool description says: \"Call after initialization_handshake and after asking which boards the user wants to work with now. Pass those ordinary familiar names here; pass NULL only to inspect inventory before the user answers.\"\n\nThe `connection_assignments` parameter: \"an object\" â€” presumably mapping board names to connection choice IDs. The serial_choices give choice_id = stable_usb_identity. So I can assign:\n- STM-A â†’ `066FFF514988525067233337` (COM12)\n- STM-B â†’ `0668FF514988525067213913` (COM17)\n\nThis is exactly the manager-supplied electronic identity mapping from RESOURCE_ASSIGNMENT.md. The zero-operator policy says the declared fixed fixtures and their stable electronic identities are \"supplied facts\" â€” I don't need to ask the user to confirm what's already recorded in the manager's assignment.\n\nLet me retry setup_overview with connection_assignments mapping the two STM boards to their declaredserial identities.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
