{"type":"assistant","uuid":"11f708b5-3cdf-45be-a050-ce4470a6e1cc","session_id":"fab1830e-aa74-488e-8a22-42b2dc0b9084","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"11f708b5-3cdf-45be-a050-ce4470a6e1cc","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash:0731-cloud","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The error says \"connection_assignments must contain exactly every familiar name\". So the keys must be the familiar names (STM-A, STM-B), and the values must be \"unique current server connection IDs\". My first attempt had keys = familiar names and values = stable USB identities, which failed with \"connection assignments must be unique current server connection IDs\". My second attempt had keys = familiar names, values = COM ports, same error. Third attempt reversed keys/values, error changed to \"must contain exactly every familiar name\" â€” meaning keys must be the familiar names.\n\nSo the values must be \"current server connection IDs\" â€” not the stable USB identity, not the port path. The serial_choices list has choice_id = stable_usb_identity. Hmm, but the error says \"unique current server connection IDs\". Maybe the connection IDs are different from the stable USB identity â€” perhaps the server has a separate connection inventory (probe connections) distinct from serial choices. The setup_overview response had \"connections\": [] â€” empty. So there are no current server connections (no probes connected via the server's connection tracking), only serial choices.\n\nWait â€” the response said \"There are more requested board names than visible debug connections.\" with connections: []. The serial_choices are UART ports, not debug connections. The server tracks debug connections separately (probes). The inventory shows no debug connections currently. So the connection_assignments parameter expects debug connection IDs, and there are none.\n\nHmm, but the serial_choices include the two STM ST-Link VCOM ports. The server's setup_overview says \"connections\": [] â€” no debug connections. So maybe the server needs the probes to be enumerated as debug connections first. But the tool description says \"Other visible debug probes may remain unassigned.\"\n\nLet me re-read the setup_overview description: \"Inventory profiles/connections and route user-provided familiar board names. Call after initialization_handshake and after asking which boards the user wants to work with now. Pass those ordinary familiar names here; pass NULL only to inspect inventory before the user answers. Other visible debug probes may remain unassigned. The normalized literal sentinel \"no board\" must be passed by itself and is never a board name candidate. If it is mixed with names, re-ask the user conversationally. A complete matching profile routes to validation, an incomplete same-identity profile to repair, and a stable-map problem to safety refresh. Unknown names receive a server-generated board_id plus setup questions. Follow only the exact route returned here. Relay only agent_prompt and friendly choices, never raw identifiers or this JSON.\"\n\nThe connection_assignments parameter: \"connection_assignments\": {\"type\": \"object\"} â€” no schema detail. The error messages tell us: values must be \"unique current server connection IDs\" and keys must be \"exactly every familiar name\".\n\nSo the mapping is {familiar_name: connection_id}. The connection IDs must be current server connection IDs. The serial inventory choice_id values are \"0668FF514988525067213913\" etc. â€” those are stable USB identities, which the server calls \"stable_usb_identity\". Are those the \"connection IDs\"? My first attempt used exactly those as values and got \"connection assignments must be unique current server connection IDs\". That error could mean the values are not recognized as current connection IDs (i.e., they're not in the server's connection inventory), OR that they're not unique (they are unique though).\n\nWait â€” maybe the issue is t