etup route.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me re-read the setup_overview response ONE more time:\n\n\"agent_prompt\": \"There are more requested board names than visible debug connections. Clarify which requested boards are currently attached before setup or validation; do not expose machine IDs. Unrelated visible probes do not need board names.\"\n\n\"connections\": [], \"profiles\": [], \"routes\": [], \"serial_choices\": [4 items], \"status\": \"setup_assignment_clarification_required\"\n\nSo the server sees 4 serial ports (2 STM + 2 J-Link). The server wants me to clarify which of the 4 are the requested boards. The connection_assignments param maps familiar names â†’ connection IDs. The connection IDs are the serial choice_ids (the only IDs the server exposed).\n\nMy first attempt used exactly those choice_ids. It failed with \"must be unique current server connection IDs\".\n\nWait â€” maybe the server's validation is that the values must be in the `connections` array, and the `connections` array is populated from the serial_choices ONLY when the user passes the names WITHOUT assignments first. So the flow is:\n1. Call with names â†’ server populates connections from serial_choices? No, connections is still empty.\n\nHmm, OR maybe the server's `connections` array is populated by the server's probe enumeration (pyDAG), and the STM probes are NOT visible to pyDAG. The serial_choices are from pyserial. So the server sees the STM VCOMs but not the STM debug probes.\n\nIf the server can't see the STM debug probes, then the setup route (which needs the probe) would fail. But the spec says the probes are connected. Maybe the server's pyDAG enumeration needs a refresh, or the server's a different enumeration.\n\nActually â€” you know what, let me just try the board_setup-plan all-NULL call. The server's guidance for setup might reveal the correct flow and the connection IDs. The board_setup-plan is the setup-routing plan for unknown names. The server's setup_overview said \"Unknown names receive a server-generated board_id plus setup questions\" â€” but my names call returned \"setup_assignment_clarification_required\" instead of a setup route. So the server wants clarification first.\n\nLet me try the connection_assignments with the choice_id values ONE more time, but this time let me be very careful about the exact strings. From the response:\n- \"choice_id\": \"0668FF514988525067213913\" â€” COM17\n- \"choice_id\": \"066FFF514988525067233337\" â€” COM12\n\nI passed:\n{\"STM-A\": \"066FFF514988525067233337\", \"STM-B\": \"0668FF514988525067213913\"}\n\nHmm wait, actually â€” maybe the server expects the connection_assignments to map familiar names to the serial choice_id, but the server's validation is that the values must be in the `connections` array, and the `connections` array is populated by the server's probe enumeration which found nothing. So the server genuinely has no debug connections.\n\nIn that case, the correct next step per the server's guidance might be to just confirm the boards are attached (via the serials) and proceed to setup. But the connection_assignments mechanism is failing.\n\nLet me try calling setup_overview with the names again â€” maybe the server's state changed after the first call (the server might have enumerated the probes). If the second call returns a setup route, great.\n\nActually, I realize I should be more careful about the retry policy: \"No unchanged failure retry; at most one corrected retry per setup step and two bounded 120-second inventory/validation attempts after a changed fact.\" The connection_assignments attempts are different formats (changed facts), so they're allowed. But I should be systematic.\n\nLet me try the board_setup-plan all-NULL call to get the server's setup guidance. This is the documented route for unknown names.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"b918e536-2acf-441a-afbb-da026a3d9695","session_id":"fab1830e-aa74-488e-8a22-42b2dc0b9084","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"b918e536-2acf-441a-afbb-da026a3d9695","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash:0731-cloud","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The server's `connection_assignments` expects \"current server connection IDs\" â€” the serial choice IDs and port paths were both rejected, and the `connections` array is empty. Let me consult the `board_setup-plan` all-NULL route, which is the server-directed path for unknown names, to understand the correct connection mechanism."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
